      <description align="left" color="orange" colored="true" height="265" resized="true" width="474" x="12" y="330">You may find the demo video &lt;a href="https://academy.rapidminer.com/learn/video/basic-etl-demo"&gt;here!&lt;br&gt;&lt;/a&gt;1. Bring the Filter Examples operator into the original process&lt;br&gt;2. Filter on Age &amp;gt;= 15&lt;br&gt;3. Add an entry&lt;br&gt;4. Filter on Age &amp;lt;= 99&lt;br&gt;5. Make sure that 'Match All' is selected&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;(Alternate Solution: Filter with Turbo Prep)&lt;br&gt;1. Run the existing process and then in results, Open in Turbo Prep&lt;br&gt;2. Right-Click on Age, then Transformations - Filter: &amp;gt;= 15&lt;br&gt;3. With Age still highlighted, Filter: &amp;lt;= 99&lt;br&gt;4. Commit Transformation&lt;br&gt;5. Add to Process&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
